# The Lintl PHPStan bridge's registration (architecture doc §17.1 Q1):
# the diagnostics rule runs once per analysed file (PHPStan's own FileNode,
# which fires for every file the analyser visits) and turns the recorded
# compiler diagnostics of compiled Lintl artifacts into PHPStan errors
# reported against the source `.lintl.php` path and line. The type half
# is data, not code: {@see \Lintl\PhpStan\Bridge} writes signature stub
# files next to the artifacts it compiles, and a consumer's phpstan.neon
# points `stubFiles` at them — so component calls in the compiled PHP (the
# exact output the CLI/LSP use, single source of truth) are type-checked
# against the signatures the scanner recorded.
services:
    -
        class: Lintl\PhpStan\LintlDiagnosticsRule
        tags: [phpstan.rules.rule]
